  "id": "Compound::DB00655 - Gene::6462",
  "verbalization": "Estrone is implicated in the binding of Shbg through multiple pathways, with the core mechanism involving steroid hormone interaction. Pathway 1 links Estrone to Norethindrone, which binds Shbg, while Pathway 2 connects Estrone to Estriol, which also binds Shbg. Pathway 3 reveals that Estrone resembles Formestane, which in turn resembles Norethindrone, both of which bind Shbg. This suggests a broader class of compounds that share structural similarities with Norethindrone and thus interact with Shbg. The lowest common ancestors across these paths—Estrone and Norethindrone—both belong to the Oxo Steroid class, reinforcing the shared mechanism of steroid hormone binding. The evidence supports a relationship where Estrone, through its structural and functional similarities to Norethindrone, indirectly influences Shbg binding, highlighting a potential role in hormone-related processes.",
